<title>HONG KONG: Hanil Bank seen planning US$200 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>Hanil Bank seen planning US$200 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hanil Bank plans to issue a US$200 million floating rate note issue, sources close to the transaction said.</p>
<p>The facility will have a final maturity of three years with no put or call options.</p>
<p>The issue will be priced at 99.97 to float at 21 basis points over the six-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for top-tier managers will be about 26 basis points.</p>
<p>A formal mandate to arrange the issue has not been offered to banks yet. -- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2847 4039</p>
</text>
